{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/svelte-query"},{"type":"text","value":" package offers a 1st-class API for using TanStack Query via Svelte."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrating from stores to the runes syntax? See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./migrate-from-v5-to-v6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"migration guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Include the QueryClientProvider near the root of your project:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import Example from './lib/Example.svelte'\n\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n</script>\n\n<QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n  <Example />\n</QueryClientProvider>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then call any function (e.g. createQuery) from any component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n\n  const query = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodos(),\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#if query.isPending}\n    <p>Loading...</p>\n  {:else if query.isError}\n    <p>Error: {query.error.message}</p>\n  {:else if query.isSuccess}\n    {#each query.data as todo}\n      <p>{todo.title}</p>\n    {/each}\n  {/if}\n</div>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"sveltekit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SvelteKit"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using SvelteKit, please have a look at "},{"type":"link","href":"./ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR & SvelteKit"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"available-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte Query offers useful functions and components that will make managing server state in Svelte apps easier."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQuery"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQueries"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createInfiniteQuery"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMutation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueryClient"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useIsFetching"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useIsMutating"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMutationState"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useIsRestoring"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHydrate"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<QueryClientProvider>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<HydrationBoundary>"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"important-differences-between-svelte-query-react-query","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important Differences between Svelte Query & React Query"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte Query offers an API similar to React Query, but there are some key differences to be mindful of."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The arguments to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions must be wrapped in a function to preserve reactivity."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"sveltekit","text":"SvelteKit","level":2},{"id":"available-functions","text":"Available Functions","level":2},{"id":"important-differences-between-svelte-query-react-query","text":"Important Differences between Svelte Query & React Query","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-query` package offers a 1st-class API for using TanStack Query via Svelte.\n\n> Migrating from stores to the runes syntax? See the [migration guide](./migrate-from-v5-to-v6).\n\n## Example\n\nInclude the QueryClientProvider near the root of your project:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import Example from './lib/Example.svelte'\n\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n</script>\n\n<QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n  <Example />\n</QueryClientProvider>\n```\n\nThen call any function (e.g. createQuery) from any component:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n\n  const query = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodos(),\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#if query.isPending}\n    <p>Loading...</p>\n  {:else if query.isError}\n    <p>Error: {query.error.message}</p>\n  {:else if query.isSuccess}\n    {#each query.data as todo}\n      <p>{todo.title}</p>\n    {/each}\n  {/if}\n</div>\n```\n\n## SvelteKit\n\nIf you are using SvelteKit, please have a look at [SSR & SvelteKit](./ssr).\n\n## Available Functions\n\nSvelte Query offers useful functions and components that will make managing server state in Svelte apps easier.\n\n- `createQuery`\n- `createQueries`\n- `createInfiniteQuery`\n- `createMutation`\n- `useQueryClient`\n- `useIsFetching`\n- `useIsMutating`\n- `useMutationState`\n- `useIsRestoring`\n- `useHydrate`\n- `<QueryClientProvider>`\n- `<HydrationBoundary>`\n\n## Important Differences between Svelte Query & React Query\n\nSvelte Query offers an API similar to React Query, but there are some key differences to be mindful of.\n\n- The arguments to the `create*` functions must be wrapped in a function to preserve reactivity.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: overview\ntitle: Overview\n---\n\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-query` package offers a 1st-class API for using TanStack Query via Svelte.\n\n> Migrating from stores to the runes syntax? See the [migration guide](./migrate-from-v5-to-v6).\n\n## Example\n\nInclude the QueryClientProvider near the root of your project:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import Example from './lib/Example.svelte'\n\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n</script>\n\n<QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n  <Example />\n</QueryClientProvider>\n```\n\nThen call any function (e.g. createQuery) from any component:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n\n  const query = createQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodos(),\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#if query.isPending}\n    <p>Loading...</p>\n  {:else if query.isError}\n    <p>Error: {query.error.message}</p>\n  {:else if query.isSuccess}\n    {#each query.data as todo}\n      <p>{todo.title}</p>\n    {/each}\n  {/if}\n</div>\n```\n\n## SvelteKit\n\nIf you are using SvelteKit, please have a look at [SSR & SvelteKit](./ssr).\n\n## Available Functions\n\nSvelte Query offers useful functions and components that will make managing server state in Svelte apps easier.\n\n- `createQuery`\n- `createQueries`\n- `createInfiniteQuery`\n- `createMutation`\n- `useQueryClient`\n- `useIsFetching`\n- `useIsMutating`\n- `useMutationState`\n- `useIsRestoring`\n- `useHydrate`\n- `<QueryClientProvider>`\n- `<HydrationBoundary>`\n\n## Important Differences between Svelte Query & React Query\n\nSvelte Query offers an API similar to React Query, but there are some key differences to be mindful of.\n\n- The arguments to the `create*` functions must be wrapped in a function to preserve reactivity.\n"}
